# Build-context filter for ERP/Dockerfile ONLY.
#
# The build runs from the repository root (`docker build -f ERP/Dockerfile .`).
# BuildKit reads this file, named after the Dockerfile, INSTEAD of the root
# .dockerignore - which belongs to the CRM image and is not modified.
#
# A whitelist rather than a blacklist: everything is excluded, then only the
# three inputs the API image copies are let back in. A new directory added to
# the repository tomorrow - generated exports, a notebook, a .env in a new
# place - stays out of the context without anyone having to remember it.

*

!requirements.txt
!ERP/config.py
!ERP/app/

# Re-excluded inside the whitelisted tree (later lines win).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
